# ==============================================================================
# TRINITY PARAMETER SCHEMA + DEFAULTS  —  AUTO-GENERATED, DO NOT EDIT BY HAND
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is generated from the ParamSpec registry:
#     trinity/_input/registry.py
# Regenerate after changing a spec:
#     python -m tools.gen_default_param --write
#
# Roles (unchanged): (1) SCHEMA — the complete set of valid parameter names;
# any key not listed here is rejected by read_param.py. (2) DEFAULTS — every
# value here is used when a user .param omits the key.
#
# To configure a run, create a .param file under param/ and override only the
# keys you need. Human-facing parameter docs (units, allowed values, physics):
# see https://jiaweiteh.github.io/trinity-web/?view=docs&page=parameters
# ==============================================================================



# ==============================================================================
# Administrative & Logging
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Specifies the model name, which serves as the prefix for all output filenames.
model_name    default

# INFO: Defines the output directory where all generated files will be stored.
path2output    def_dir

# INFO: Output-format selector; currently inert — snapshots are always written as JSONL.
output_format    JSON

# INFO: Target number of points retained for simplified profile arrays in saved snapshots (bubble_T_arr, bubble_n_arr, bubble_dTdr_arr, bubble_v_arr, shell_grav_force_m, shell_n_arr). Default 100. Larger values give higher-fidelity snapshots at the cost of larger output files. Clamped to >= 20 (matches the coverage-skeleton chunk count). The first two simplify calls per implicit-phase snapshot log their reconstruction R² at INFO level so you can verify the chosen budget is faithful.
simplify_npoints    100

# INFO: Write the simplified profile arrays (bubble_T/n/dTdr/v, shell_n, shell_grav) into every N-th snapshot row: 1 = every row (the historical output), 0 = never (scalars only; rows are 86 % smaller; for surveys that read scalars). A row without arrays lacks the log_*/_r_arr keys and the Cloudy exporter refuses it by name. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/output-profiles/PLAN.md E5.
profile_every    1

# INFO: Also write every N-th row's profile arrays at full resolution, before any simplification, to <path2output>/profiles_full/row<id>.npz (numpy savez_compressed, float64, about 1-2 MB per row): 0 = never. The audit's ground truth and the source for consumers that need the full shape (TrinityOutput.profile_full). Same PLAN.md, E2.
profile_dump_every    0

# INFO: Logging level for terminal and file output. Controls how much detail is logged. DEBUG emits per-RHS-evaluation records (formatted and written to the log file on every solver stage), a measurable hot-path cost over a full run; INFO is the default, DEBUG is opt-in for diagnostics.
log_level    INFO

# INFO: Enable console (terminal) output for logging. If True, log messages are printed to terminal.
log_console    False

# INFO: Enable file output for logging. If True, log messages are written to a .log file in the output directory.
log_file    True

# INFO: Use colored output in terminal. If True, log messages are color-coded by severity (DEBUG=cyan, INFO=green, WARNING=yellow, ERROR=red, CRITICAL=magenta).
log_colors    True

# INFO: Energy-implicit (beta, delta) solver: 'hybr' (default; unbounded scipy root-finder with a physical dMdt>0 acceptance gate) or 'legacy' (bounded grid + L-BFGS-B).
betadelta_solver    hybr

# INFO: Opt-in: when phase 1b's beta-delta guess and the +-0.02 rescue grid have no physical bubble structure, seed hybr from the best physical point of a coarse (beta, delta) map (docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/early-1b/F1_ADOPTION.md). False (default) = unchanged.
betadelta_wide_search    False

# INFO: How the integration starts. 'weaver' (default, shipped): from the free-streaming wind into phase 1a (get_InitPhaseParam.get_y0); refused with a ValueError when the first structure solve would fall off the non-CIE cooling cube (phi(r0) = Qi/(4 pi r0^2) > 1e21 cm^-2 s^-1: a weak wind in a dense core). 'stromgren' (phii_scheme 'swept' only): phases 1a-1c are skipped and the swept momentum phase starts at the end of the R-type phase, r_s = R_St (solved on the run's own density profile), u = 2 c_i/sqrt(3), M_s = M(<R_St), the wind bubble inside at its ram-pressure equilibrium (Hosokawa & Inutsuka 2006 eq. 36; Lancaster et al. 2025a sec. 3.5); refused at zeta = R_eq/R_St >= 1 or R_St > rCloud. 'auto' (opt-in, rule A1): the Weaver start where its seed has a physical bubble structure (phase 1a's first structure solve, else get_betadelta's 77-point wide-search map), else the Stroemgren start where it applies (swept, zeta_MD < 1, R_St <= rCloud), else refused with both reasons; outside phii_scheme swept always the Weaver start; a Weaver start under 'auto' runs with betadelta_wide_search True unless the .param sets that key; metadata.json records the start used. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/PLAN.md, weak-wind/start-selection/AUTO_START.md.
start_scheme    weaver

# INFO: Phase 1b: when the beta-delta solve fails with a structure-solve failure (hybr left the integrable domain, e.g. at a steep feedback ramp), retry once from the beta that balances the energy equation at the previous segment's losses (A12 inverted); the result is kept only if it is a physical, converged root, and found condensation roots are never retried. False restores the pre-2026-11 behaviour (hold the old beta/delta). docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/early-1b/G1_PLAN.md.
betadelta_balance_retry    True


# ==============================================================================
# Physical Parameters
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: The mass of the molecular cloud.
# UNIT: [Msun]
mCloud    1e7

# INFO: Star formation efficiency.
sfe    0.01

# INFO: Cloud metallicity
# UNIT: [Zsun]
ZCloud    1

# INFO: Include the photoionised-gas pressure P_HII in P_drive. When False, P_HII is set to zero. Since 2026-08-14 (C3c) P_HII is NOT the capped-Strömgren shell pressure it used to be — that quantity was an algebraic relabelling of the confining pressure, carrying no dependence on Qi. It is now a confinement regime switch on the CAVITY Strömgren density (get_bubbleParams.get_phii_c3c): exactly 0.0 while the ionised gas is confined, because a confined skin transmits the confining pressure rather than adding to it, and the cavity photoionised pressure once confinement cannot hold it. True and False differ only where the unconfined branch fires. At nominal wind that is rare before the momentum phase (P_C3a/Pb <= 0.04 in the energy and implicit phases of B3MW3 and B3MW10); at weak wind it fires inside the energy phase (B3MW001: from t = 1.2 kyr, and on every implicit row). Irrelevant to the momentum phase under phii_scheme swept, which has no P_HII.
include_PHII    True

# INFO: Closed fraction of the bubble wall (covering fraction Cf). Geometry-set energy/mass leak: hot gas vents through the open area (1-Cf)*4*pi*R2^2 at the interior sound speed, draining bubble energy (and, when the mass sink is enabled, mass). Cf=1 recovers the sealed (Weaver) bubble exactly; not fragmentation-triggered. Usable range ~0.9-0.99; Cf near 0 drains the bubble within a step and stresses the integrator.
coverFraction    1.0

# INFO: On by default: the shell holds the swept mass minus the gas conduction has evaporated into the bubble. True: in phases 1b and 1c the bubble's mass (bubble_mass, the structure solve's integral; held at 1b's last value through 1c) is taken off the swept mass wherever the shell's mass acts -- the shell solve's mass condition (so rShell, and under phii_scheme swept the R2 root, see the net mass), the inertia and weight in the equation of motion (the evaporated gas pulling from inside R2), and swept's 1b hand-off momentum. The subtraction starts once the bubble holds less than the swept mass (a weak wind whose phase 1a lasts ~1 yr enters 1b with more; until then the shell keeps it). Phase 1a is unchanged (early in 1a the bubble's structure holds more than the shell has swept, so the subtraction would leave no shell), and at the momentum hand-off the gas returns to the shell. Once started, a bubble holding the whole swept mass leaves no shell and is refused (ValueError). shell_mass stays the swept mass; the net mass is shell_mass - bubble_mass on 1b/1c rows. False = the swept mass stays whole in the shell (the behaviour before 2026-11). docs/dev/phii-identity/mass-budget/PLAN.md.
shell_mass_net    True

# INFO: Hydrogen nuclei number density of cloud core (n_H). Standard GMC/ISM convention. Mass density: rho = nCore * mu_convert * m_H. If `densPL` AND densPL_alpha = 0, this is the average cloud density.
# UNIT: [cm**-3]
nCore    1e5

# INFO: Hydrogen nuclei number density of the ambient ISM (n_H). Mass density: rho = nISM * mu_convert * m_H.
# UNIT: [cm**-3]
nISM    1

# INFO: Core radius of the molecular cloud.
# UNIT: [pc]
rCore    0.01

# INFO: Maximum plausible cloud radius used by the pre-run GMC parameter validation. If the computed rCloud exceeds this, the run is rejected as implausibly diffuse for the given mass. Increase to allow larger, more diffuse clouds.
# UNIT: [pc]
rCloud_max    200

# INFO: Which P_HII closure to use. 'c3c' (default, shipped): the confinement regime switch on the CAVITY Stroemgren density -- exactly 0.0 while the ionised gas is confined, P_C3a once it is not (get_bubbleParams.get_phii_c3c). 'front' (option C, D16 ruled 2026-09-11): the pressure AT the ionisation front, (mu_c/mu_i)*n_IF*k_B*T_ion, applied by the caller over 4*pi*R_IF**2 on the neutral rind with NO Pb or P_ram added, and exactly 0.0 on a fully ionised shell (get_bubbleParams.get_phii_front). The two differ in area, in composition and in which body is driven, so they are not interchangeable magnitudes -- see  'o1' and 'k11' are MEASURED CANDIDATES, not options: both drive the neutral rind over 4*pi*R_IF**2 like 'front' but source the skin density differently -- 'o1' from the shell's inner boundary (P_conf/p_ref), 'k11' from Geen 2019's coupled wind+photon root. O1 FAILS the photoionisation-only limit by construction (test_phii_limits.py L1/L1b/L2) and is kept only so that result stays measurable; do not select it for science. See docs/dev/phii-identity/PLAN.md 0.0.5 Step 3. 'swept' (PLAN.md 0.0.11, Steps 4-6, 2026-10-22/25): the swept-mass formulation in the IMPLICIT, TRANSITION and MOMENTUM phases -- the shell's outer radius r_s and its gas speed u are evolved, the mass is the cloud mass inside r_s, R2 is root-found each segment so the shell solve ends at r_s, and the drive is the profile's own outer pressure (no P_HII); the outer edge runs at the isothermal-jump speed where the gas ahead is warm cloud gas, and at the gas speed past rCloud (rs_dot). In the implicit phase the inner pressure is the bubble's own (switch-on ramp included) and the beta/delta solve sees the bubble wall's speed dR2/dt from successive roots (cool_alpha = t dR2/dt / R2); in transition the inner pressure is max(P_th, P_ram) and its energy equation sees the same wall speed. The energy phase (1a) is c3c; swept takes over at 1b entry (trinity/phase2_momentum/swept.py).
phii_scheme    c3c


# ==============================================================================
# Density Profile
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Specifies how the cloud density scales with radius.
dens_profile    densPL

# INFO: if `densBE` is selected, then the ratio `Omega = nCore/nCloudEdge` must be specified.
densBE_Omega    14.1

# INFO: if `densPL` is selected, then the power-law coefficient `nCore*(r/rCore)^alpha` (0 = homogeneous, -2 = isothermal) must be specified.
densPL_alpha    0


# ==============================================================================
# Termination Conditions
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Allow shell dissolution to terminate simulation. If False, shell dissolution check is disabled.
allowShellDissolution    True

# INFO: Duration (in Myr) that shell_nMax must remain below nISM before dissolution is triggered.
# UNIT: [Myr]
stop_t_diss    1

# INFO: Maximum radial extent permitted for shell expansion. Set to None to disable this termination condition.
# UNIT: [pc]
stop_r    500

# INFO: Maximum duration of the simulation. Set to None to disable this termination condition.
# UNIT: [Myr]
stop_t    15

# INFO: Terminate simulation after the shell crosses the cloud edge (R2 > rCloud). Value is the number of post-crossing segment-loop snapshots to record before terminating. Set to None to disable. 0 stops at the edge (1a reconciliation snapshot only). N>0 lets the implicit phase advance for N more segments past the crossing — note the implicit phase's end-of-phase reconciliation snapshot adds one extra past-rCloud sample, so the total snapshots with R2 >= rCloud is roughly N + 2 (1 at-edge + N in-loop + 1 recon).
stop_at_rCloud_nSnap    None

# INFO: Collapse radius cap. A shell moving inward ends the run as collapsed below collapse_radius = min(coll_r, coll_r_frac * R2_max).
# UNIT: [pc]
coll_r    1

# INFO: Collapse radius as a fraction of the largest radius the shell has reached: collapse_radius = min(coll_r, coll_r_frac * R2_max), so a shell that never grew past a few pc is not stopped at coll_r on its first inward swing. The radius used and which term set it are written to collapse_radius and collapse_rule. A very large value (e.g. 1e9) leaves coll_r alone.
coll_r_frac    0.1


# ==============================================================================
# Stellar Feedback (SPS)
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Stellar-rotation flag. Selects rot vs norot non-CIE cooling tables (trinity/cooling/non_CIE/read_cloudy.py). Only rot tables ship in lib/default/opiate/, so 0 (norot) requires the user to supply matching cooling tables and an sps_path pointing at a norot SPS file; the default SPS fallback rejects SB99_rotation=0. NOTE: name retained for stability. May rename to sps_rotation in a future PR once the cooling subsystem stops being SB99-flavored.
SB99_rotation    1

# INFO: Reference cluster mass used in f_mass = mCluster / sps_refmass.
# UNIT: [Msun]
sps_refmass    def_value

# INFO: Fraction of cold mass entrained in stellar winds (increases Mdot_wind, reduces velocity).
FB_mColdWindFrac    0

# INFO: Fraction of cold mass entrained in supernova ejecta (increases Mdot_SN, reduces velocity).
FB_mColdSNFrac    0

# INFO: Defines the thermalization efficiency for colliding stellar winds.
FB_thermCoeffWind    1

# INFO: Defines the thermalization efficiency for supernova ejecta.
FB_thermCoeffSN    1

# INFO: How the SPS table is interpolated in time. 'pchip' (default): monotone, never outside the two bracketing table rows, so the feedback is never negative; total = wind + supernova. 'cubic': the spline used before 2026-11, kept only to reproduce older runs; it rings across the supernova switch-on and switch-off (negative mechanical luminosity near 3.45 Myr at FB_thermCoeffWind 0.01 and near 45 Myr at every coefficient). docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/early-1b/SPS_TRANSIENTS.md.
sps_interp    pchip

# INFO: Specifies the velocity of supernova ejecta.
# UNIT: [km * s**-1]
FB_vSN    1e4

# INFO: Full path to an SPS data file. If def_path (default), TRINITY uses
sps_path    def_path

sps_col_t    def_unset

sps_col_Qi    def_unset

sps_col_fi    def_unset

sps_col_Lbol    def_unset

sps_col_Lmech_W    def_unset

sps_col_pdot_W    def_unset

sps_col_Lmech_total    def_unset

sps_col_Lmech_SN    def_unset

sps_col_pdot_SN    def_unset

sps_col_Mdot_SN    def_unset

sps_col_v_SN    def_unset

sps_col_Li    def_unset

sps_col_Ln    def_unset


# ==============================================================================
# Cooling Tables
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Selects the CIE (T > 10^5.5 K) cooling curve.
path_cooling_CIE    3

# INFO: Folder containing the non-CIE (T < 10^5.5 K) OPIATE/CLOUDY cubes.
path_cooling_nonCIE    def_dir


# ==============================================================================
# Physical Constants & Microphysics
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: Mean mass per particle for neutral atomic gas (HI + He) = mu_H/(1+x_He). Derived at load from x_He (default 14/11 at x_He=0.1). In units of m_H.
# UNIT: [m_H]
mu_atom    14/11

# INFO: Mean mass per particle for the HOT bubble interior (fully ionised H+ + He2+) = mu_H/(2+x_He*(1+Z_He)). Derived at load from x_He, Z_He (default 14/23 at x_He=0.1, Z_He=2). The ~1e4 K ionised shell uses mu_ion_shell (singly-ionised He) instead. In units of m_H.
# UNIT: [m_H]
mu_ion    14/23

# INFO: Mean mass per particle for molecular gas (H2 + He) = mu_H/(0.5+x_He). Derived at load from x_He (default 14/6 at x_He=0.1). In units of m_H.
# UNIT: [m_H]
mu_mol    14/6

# INFO: Mass per hydrogen nucleus mu_H = (1+4*x_He) (=1.4 at x_He=0.1), in units of m_H. Use for the n_H -> rho mass conversion (rho = mu_convert * n_H); independent of ionisation state. Derived at load from x_He. All densities n in TRINITY are hydrogen-nuclei densities n_H.
# UNIT: [m_H]
mu_convert    1.4

# INFO: Helium-to-hydrogen number ratio n_He/n_H. Composition source of truth: mu_atom, mu_ion, mu_mol, mu_convert and chi_e are all derived from x_He and Z_He at load (read_param Step 6).
x_He    0.1

# INFO: Helium ionisation state in the HOT bubble interior (T~1e6-1e7 K): 2 = doubly ionised (He2+). Sets mu_ion and the bubble electron factor chi_e = 1 + Z_He*x_He.
Z_He    2

# INFO: Helium ionisation state in the ~1e4 K ionised shell / HII region: 1 = singly ionised (He+). Sets mu_ion_shell and chi_e_shell = 1 + Z_He_shell*x_He. (He2+ needs ~1e5 K, so the photoionised shell is singly ionised.)
Z_He_shell    1

# INFO: Temperature of the neutral shell gas behind the ionisation front [K], or 'auto' (the default since 2026-11-02, docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/PDR_DEFAULT_PLAN.md P5): the atomic (PDR) zone's temperature is the PDR surface temperature of Kaufman et al. 1999 (lib/default/pdr/k99_tsurf_grid.csv) at the front's far-UV field (fFUV_Ln x Ln) and pressure-continuous density; the table's 5000 K top lies outside K99's outermost contour, so there (young, dense, strongly irradiated shells) it is a lower bound. H2 forms from Bialy & Sternberg 2016's column to the H/H2 transition on (warm H2 at that temperature until tauShell_mol, cold at TShell_mol beyond); each row stores shell_T_atom, shell_G0_IF and shell_N_tran. 'auto' needs TShell_mol > 0. A number with TShell_mol > 0: the atomic zone's temperature, e.g. 300 K. A number with TShell_mol 0: one neutral zone, the layer of runs before 2026-11-02 (100 K was the default); the layer's structure sees only T/mu (mu_atom), and the value is an EFFECTIVE thickness parameter for a warm PDR skin plus cold molecular gas, not a temperature: an isobaric layer's thickness is the sum over zones of (T/mu) N, so a neutral column N_neu whose first N_tr = tauShell_mol/dust_sigma (2e21 cm^-2 at the defaults) is atomic at T_PDR and whose rest is molecular at T_mol has the thickness of one zone at T_eff = f T_PDR + (1 - f) (mu_atom/mu_mol) T_mol, f = min(1, N_tr/N_neu): with 300 K / 20 K that is 300 K for N_neu <= 2e21, 83 K at 8e21, 10.9 K as N_neu grows (the 7c-1 ladder's shells span 7e19 to 7e25 cm^-2). docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/PLAN.md.
TShell_neu    auto

# INFO: Temperature of the molecular zone of the neutral shell [K]. 20 K by default since 2026-11-02 (PDR_DEFAULT_PLAN.md P5; Krumholz, McKee & Tumlinson 2009): beyond a dust optical depth tauShell_mol behind the ionisation front the shell gas is molecular (mu_mol) at this temperature, with the pressure-continuous density jump n_mol = n_atom (mu_mol/mu_atom) (T_atom/TShell_mol) (27.5 at 300 K / 20 K, x_He 0.1). Thermal pressure only: magnetic support would thicken the zone (Pellegrini et al. 2007, 2009); an effective value can stand in for it. 0 = one neutral zone at TShell_neu, which must then be a number: the layer of runs before 2026-11-02. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/PLAN.md.
TShell_mol    20

# INFO: Dust optical depth of the atomic (PDR) zone behind the ionisation front at which the neutral shell turns molecular: the shell march's own tau (dtau/dr = n dust_sigma), so the column is tauShell_mol/dust_sigma (2.0e21 cm^-2, A_V 1.07 at the defaults) and it scales with metallicity as the H/H2 transition does (Sternberg et al. 2014 eq. 40: a fixed dust optical depth ln(alpha G/2 + 1)). Used only when TShell_mol > 0. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/PLAN.md.
tauShell_mol    3

# INFO: Far-UV (6-13.6 eV) share of the non-ionising luminosity Ln, for the PDR's field at the ionisation front when TShell_neu is 'auto' (step (b)). An ESTIMATE that can be far off: Kim et al. 2023 (ApJS 264, 10) Fig. 21, read by pixel, gives 0.65-0.7 for a Starburst99 cluster of 0-5.5 Myr; unknown later. A stellar table's own far-UV column is to replace it when one exists (PDR_DEFAULT_PLAN.md D-B3). docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/neutral-shell/PDR_DEFAULT_PLAN.md.
fFUV_Ln    0.67

# INFO: Temperature of the ionised shell region. 8000 K (maintainer ruling 2026-09-06, PLAN.md W62): the two published Te-metallicity relations give 7584 K (Shaver+1983) and 7009 K (Mendez-Delgado+2023) at solar Z (Balser & Wenger 2024). NOT universal -- harder fields and higher densities push Te up. caseB_alpha is rescaled from this value by (T/1e4)^-0.83 (Draine 2011, ApJ 732, 100) in read_param, so the two cannot drift apart.
TShell_ion    8e3

# INFO: Dust cross-section at solar metallicity.
# UNIT: [cm**2]
dust_sigma    1.5e-21

# INFO: Metallicity below which there is effectively no dust
# UNIT: [Zsun]
dust_noZ    0.05

# INFO: The Rosseland mean dust opacity kappa_IR.
# UNIT: [cm**2 * g**-1]
dust_KappaIR    4

# INFO: The case B recombination coefficient
# UNIT: [cm**3 * s**-1]
caseB_alpha    2.59e-13

# INFO: the adiabatic index
gamma_adia    5/3

# INFO: The thermal conduction coefficient C
# UNIT: [erg * s**-1 * cm**-1 * K**(-7/2)]
C_thermal    6e-7

# INFO: speed of light
# UNIT: [cm * s**-1]
c_light    29979245800

# INFO: Gravitational constant
# UNIT: [cm**3 * g**-1 * s**-2]
G    6.6743e-08

# INFO: Boltzmann constant
# UNIT: [erg * K**-1]
k_B    1.380649e-16

# INFO: ISM Pressure, P/k
# UNIT: [K * cm**-3]
PISM    0

# INFO: Temperature of the cloud's own (molecular) gas, for its thermal pressure on the shell INSIDE the cloud: (mu_convert/mu_mol) n(r) k_B TCloud while every ionising photon is absorbed (density_profile.get_press_cloud). Default 10 K (cold molecular gas) since 2026-10-29 (gate G-CP3); it was 0 before. 0 = no pressure from the cloud gas. Outside the cloud the ambient pressure is PISM. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/PLAN.md section 11.
# UNIT: [K]
TCloud    10

# INFO: Virial parameter of the cloud's gas for its turbulent pressure on the shell INSIDE the cloud only: rho sigma^2 with sigma^2 = alphaVirCloud G M(<r) / (5 r), Krumholz & Matzner (2009) eq. 17, alpha_vir = 5 sigma^2 r / (G M(<r)) as Bertoldi & McKee (1992), sigma the total one-dimensional dispersion (thermal included, so the term adds rho sigma^2 minus the TCloud thermal pressure); M(<r) is the cloud gas inside r, the cluster not included (density_profile.get_press_cloud). The ambient ISM outside the cloud is PISM. 0 (default) = off. Experimental. docs/dev/phii-identity/weak-wind/PLAN.md section 11.3.
alphaVirCloud    0


# ==============================================================================
# Solver / Phase Control
# ==============================================================================

# INFO: When (Lgain-Lloss)/Lgain approaches this value, begin momentum-driving phase.
phaseSwitch_LlossLgain    0.05

# INFO: Energy->momentum transition criteria, COMMA-SEPARATED (fires on whichever occurs first). Tokens: 'cooling_balance' (default = current behavior), 'blowout' (R2>rCloud), 'ebpeak' (net energy Edot_from_balance<=0); 'r1' aliases 'blowout,ebpeak'. e.g. 'cooling_balance,blowout'. Non-default sets DRIVE the R1 transition (docs/dev/transition/pt4/R1_SHADOW_PLAN.md).
transition_trigger    cooling_balance

# INFO: Opt-in unresolved-interface-cooling boost (Paper-II note, docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/PLAN.md). 'none' (default) = resolved cooling unchanged, BYTE-IDENTICAL. 'multiplier' = Lleak + cooling_boost_fmix*Lcool. 'theta_target' = max(Lcool+Lleak, cooling_boost_theta*Lmech) (tops up to a target loss fraction, single-count). The boosted loss feeds the beta-delta residual, the energy ODE, AND the transition trigger consistently. Never a (1-theta)*Lmech input rescale on top of Lcool -- that double-counts. FALLBACK: 'multiplier' is superseded for L21b *calibration* by cooling_boost_fA (docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/FA_STATE_COUPLED.md); retained as a supported opt-in mechanism and bench control arm.
cooling_boost_mode    none

# INFO: Multiplier on the resolved cooling integral when cooling_boost_mode=multiplier (f_mix >= 1). Default 1.0 = no boost. FALLBACK: superseded for L21b *calibration* by cooling_boost_fA (docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/FA_STATE_COUPLED.md); retained pending a state-coupled successor.
cooling_boost_fmix    1.0

# INFO: Target loss fraction theta = Lloss/Lmech when cooling_boost_mode=theta_target (0..1, with a ceiling theta_max<1 at GMC-core density). Default 0.0 = off.
cooling_boost_theta    0.0

# INFO: Rung-A probe (docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/KAPPA_EFF_SCOPING.md): multiplier f_kappa on the Spitzer conduction coefficient C_thermal in the bubble-structure solve (f_kappa >= 1). Inflates conduction-zone cooling THROUGH the structure (theta emerges as an output), unlike the scalar cooling_boost on Lcool. Default 1.0 = byte-identical. NOTE it RAISES the evaporative mass flux, which MATCHES El-Badry+19 Eq 47 (mdot ~ C^(2/7), C=6e-7 cgs = C_thermal): measured 1.2175 vs analytic 2^(2/7)=1.2190 at f_kappa=2. [CORRECTED 2026-07-29, FINDINGS 23: an earlier note here called that the "wrong El-Badry sign" -- it is not; Eq 47 rises with conduction. the OTHER factor of Eq 47, (1-theta)^(37/35)/theta^(2/7), falls with theta and is the channel cooling_boost_fA moves.] It remains a structural probe rather than the final model for independent reasons: no whole-band f_kappa exists (FINDINGS 12) and a scalar on Spitzer C cannot represent cool-layer mixing, where kappa_mix/kappa_Spitzer ~ 1e3-1e7 (FINDINGS 9b). Set to 'auto' to resolve at load time to the measured f_kappa that fires the cooling_balance trigger for this (mCloud, sfe, nCore), from the 819-run sweep grid (trinity/_input/fkappa_auto.py; docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/data/fkappa_nH_sweep.csv). The 'auto' grid was measured at cooling_boost_fA=1; combining with f_A!=1 silently invalidates the lookup.
cooling_boost_kappa    1.0

# INFO: Interface source-term boost f_A (docs/dev/transition/pdv-trigger/SOURCE_TERM_DESIGN.md): multiplies the net radiative dudt inside the bubble-structure ODE and the resolved L2+L3 loss integrals, in the interface band T < 10^5.5 K -- the bubble-side conduction front (zones L2+L3) draped on the contact discontinuity at R2, NOT the interface surface itself. The dudt gate is strictly T < 10^5.5 K; the L2+L3 component scaling is unconditional (a degenerate no-conduction-zone slice can scale a sliver above-band -- FINDINGS.md 15j). The 1-D projection of fractal-interface mixing (Lancaster) on the SOURCE side: cooling rises THROUGH the structure and evaporation dMdt FALLS -- the theta-channel of El-Badry Eq 47, (1-theta)^(37/35)/theta^(2/7). [CORRECTED 2026-07-29, FINDINGS 23: cooling_boost_kappa raising dMdt is NOT a contrasting "wrong sign" -- it moves the other factor of Eq 47, (C/6e-7 cgs)^(2/7), which rises with conduction by construction. Both knobs move Eq 47 correctly, in different variables.] L_leak is deliberately NOT scaled (leakage is bulk escape, not interface radiation). Requires f_A > 0; values < 1 are untested suppression territory. Default 1.0 = byte-identical. Single-knob use intended: combining with cooling_boost_mode != none or cooling_boost_kappa != 1 warns at load (double-boost / cross-knob).
cooling_boost_fA    1.0

# INFO: Scalar f_cool in [0, 1] on the resolved net radiative cooling EVERYWHERE in the bubble: the net source dudt inside the bubble-structure ODE at every temperature, and the loss integrals L1 (CIE interior) + L2 (conduction zone) + L3 (intermediate). The suppression counterpart of the cooling_boost_* family (docs/dev/cooling-enhance-suppress/PLAN.md). 1.0 (default) = shipped physics, BYTE-IDENTICAL; 0 = no radiative loss from the bubble, the conduction-only Weaver+77 structure (the energy-retaining limit); values > 1 are refused (enhancement is the boost family's job). In the non-CIE band (T < 10^5.5 K) the net term includes the cube's photoionisation heating, so the factor scales that heating too. L_leak (bulk escape), the conduction coefficient and the evaporative dMdt seed are not touched. Physically it is a bracket (the adiabatic limit), a stand-in for sub-solar metallicity, or a probe of cooling below CIE in over-ionised gas; the 3-D codes' delayed or suppressed cooling cures a numerical over-cooling that a resolved 1-D bubble does not have. Single-knob use intended: combining with cooling_boost_mode != none, cooling_boost_kappa != 1 or cooling_boost_fA != 1 warns at load.
cooling_scale    1.0

# INFO: Phase-1a integration segments as a fraction of the bubble age: dt_segment = phase1a_segFrac*(t_now-tSF). The driving terms (bubble structure, shell, P_HII) are frozen per segment, so this holds their staleness at a constant fraction of the expansion time at every object scale. Set to 0 to fall back to the fixed 30-yr SEGMENT_DURATION, which is a small step for a GMC but spans the entire free-streaming->Weaver relaxation of a compact HII region (docs/dev/phase1a-init/FINDINGS.md). Must be in [0, 1]: negative values would hit the same <=0 fallback as 0 and silently run stock segments, and above 1 a single frozen segment spans more than the bubble's whole age. Converged at the 0.03-0.3 measured range (0.1 -> 0.03 moves R2 at the compact-probe observed age by 0.11%).
phase1a_segFrac    0.1

# INFO: Cooling related values. alpha = v2*t_now/R2
cool_alpha    0.6

# INFO: Cooling related values. beta = - dPb/dt.
cool_beta    0.8

# INFO: Cooling related values. delta = dT/dt.
cool_delta    -6/35

# INFO: The relative radius xi = r/R2, at which we measure the bubble temperature.
bubble_xi_Tb    0.98
